From 0d10604c32e79563b9ffaf0b0a9da0ba813388de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Pulipaka <adipu@utexas.edu>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 03:34:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] Flex contacts as MuJoCo C: per-pair MJ_MAXCONPAIR cap,
 C's selection, all box-triangle contacts

- Geom-flex contacts are filtered like MuJoCo C's filterFlexContacts / filterPreContacts: one group per
  (world, body, flex), MJ_MAXCONPAIR contacts kept by deepest-first farthest-point sampling over the group's
  candidates in C's canonical order (plane-vertex contacts in vertex order, then geom-element contacts in
  element order; for MuJoCo 3.14 the flex BVH leaf order its midphase visits), coincident candidates allowed.
  ENABLE_GEOM_FLEX_FPS=False restores upstream's uncapped geom-flex contacts.
- FLEX_FPS_MODE: 'c314' reproduces MuJoCo C 3.14 exactly (it swaps chosen contacts to the front without
  swapping its bookkeeping), 'main' reproduces MuJoCo C after 2026-09-23 (plain FPS), 'parallel' is upstream's
  block-parallel FPS. Default follows the installed mujoco version. The serial modes run one thread per group
  in one launch (the parallel mode needs 3 launches per selected contact without conditional graphs).
- Box-triangle: all vertex and corner contacts in C's order and with C's margin tests (up to 11 per element);
  upstream kept the first 2 (BOX_TRIANGLE_ALL_CONTACTS=False restores that).
- Model.flex_elemorder: rank of each element in MuJoCo C 3.14's midphase order.
- Tests: the plane-cloth cap, trilinear trajectory counts and the FPS NumPy reference follow MuJoCo C.

Measured against MuJoCo C from synchronized states (cloth + cable on a box and on a plane, 400 steps):
contact sets equal 78/78 and 83/83, one-step qvel error <= 4.9e-5 (was 0.43-0.57 m/s with upstream's contacts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
